{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1550095-building-generic-fantasy-with-exess","id":1550095,"title":"Building Generic Fantasy with ExEss","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-13T02:33:18-07:00","id":1550095,"title":"Building Generic Fantasy with ExEss","content":"So for a while now I have been searching for some system to express some ideas I had about a Fantasy setting, and after examining a few systems, I've decided on using ExEss to do so (I just like the system, what can I say). Anyway, while it deviates from the common Exalted setting, I thought to post it here as at worst case scenario, people might find it of interest to break it apart and use it to make Exigents or something. Anyway, here's the link-<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-aW2vioyIQC-y8D-x9Dt8lXxAMAsLltprfcmj77c7qY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">XS-Generic Fantasy</a><br /> <br /> The basics are as follows-<br /> <br /> Classes: the core of the system. There are 15 power sources, with each of them having 4 associated Classes. The Power Sources are Ambient (wild magic), Arcane (scholarly magic), Cursed (dark magic), Divine (magic of the gods and faith), Dream (reality is an illusion), Enlightened (rework of &quot;Ki magic&quot;), Esoteric (stolen divine magic), False (not real magic), Fundamental (elemental magic without the elements), Hedge (sympathy magic), Liminal (magic derived from magic entities), Null (anti magic), Primal (nature magic), Psychic (psionics) and Scientific (magical science). Each power source also has a type of a magical item associated with it, giving Resonance between the users of that magic and that item.<br /> <br /> Each Class is composed of the following: methodology (how a certain Class uses their Charms/spells/martial arts/etc, with some mechanical support), resonance (the magical items they resonate with), capacity (what auxilary abilities the Class can learn, based around 2nd Circle Sorcery, 1st Circle Necromancy and Celestial Martial Arts with a 1-to-1 circle deviation being allowed to modify that base), 2 Advantages, milestone (Epic milestones take the place of Exalted milestones), and Great Curse (the conditions afflicted upon the Class beyond the common one)<br /> <br /> Auras: represents the &quot;subclass&quot;, which is some sort of a magical source the colors them magic. Basically of the Class is the system that operates the magic, the Aura is the content that flows into it in order to be produced into magic. Currently, they are meant to work as the Anima effects of the character.<br /> <br /> Ancestry: replaces races, currently uses the Exalted setting as a base. While all people come from some place, after becoming Awakened (that is, being able to use Essence through a Class), the Ancestry imbues the character with a power derived from their history and origin in a manner which most people can't access. It includes which Excellencies are available for the Class (each Ancestry has 2 associated Abilities and a Attribute) and which Ox Body they can buy.<br /> <br /> And that's the plan, basically, currently halfway through the Classes, probably will skip Auras and work on Ancestries after I'll finish the Classes. Please let me know what you think!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T00:14:28-07:00","id":1550678,"title":"","content":"Once did something along those lines with M:tAw, so long ago, even before WoD:Mirrors or the change from nWoD to CotD were things.<br /> Later on plugged some bits from Immortals, VtR and HtV to the mess in a sort of incidental crossover with Scion: Ragnarok, so to speak.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Exalted per se, i've toyed all too many times with the idea of making a sword &amp; sorcery game centered on heroic mortals messing around with Sorcery and its Workings, Thaumaturgy, Evocations, Geomancy and other supernatural bits in pursuit of their own personal paths to power and so on, lack of spiritual favor or mandate be damned. Maybe with some homebrewed bizarre crypto-lore bits about Shards as aspects of Szoreny, lost lands or worlds in the Wyld or beyond, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1377411-how-does-your-creation-vary/page10#post1405701\">Flipside </a>Creation's elusive &quot;opposite&quot; and some other nonsense mixed in.<br /> <br /> Not much to add - among other things because i've been ridiculously slow with getting fully into Exalted: Essence - but definitely going to delve into things later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-23-2025, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}